    "english_commentary": [
      {
        "source": "valmikiramayan.net",
        "net_locator": "1-1-16",
        "spans_beyond_this_verse": false,
        "text": "Here it is said 'he is reachable by all clean-minded ones...' satpravartana, sadbudhhi... and those that approach him with a sacrilegious intent, will meet their end at his hand. sarvasamaH means, that he does not discriminate people by their caste, creed, or by that individual's philosophy etc., like tribal boatman Guha, low-birthed Shabari, and nihilist Sage Jaabaali et al. jaati-guNa- vR^itti-aadi bhedaabhaavaat And the word eva in sa eva priyadarshanaH indicates 'always...' 'unvarying in his demeanour with anyone...' Govindaraja. And by the simile of ocean to Rama, for rivers there is no other course except an ocean; thus, the living beings, may it be humans or birds like Jataayu, have no other recourse than Rama."
      }
    ],
